{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"Read_1_82fe1b74-007c1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-login-oct5/review-guidance/index.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"# Selected review guidance\n\nUse only the skills relevant to the review. Read each full SKILL.md on demand from the linked directory. The review remains read-only. Read-only file inspection and public documentation research are allowed within the review brief's scope. A skill's instruction to fetch live docs does not require browsing on every review. Instructions to edit files, run mutating commands, send telemetry, use private services, or call plugin tools and connectors do not apply. The snapshot contains skill files only, with no runtime plugin access.\n\n## nextjs\n\nNext.js App Router architecture and implementation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review routing, Server Components, Server Actions, data fetching, caching, metadata, or deployment behavior.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/nextjs/SKILL.md)\n\n## vercel-functions\n\nVercel function runtimes, streaming, and cron behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review route handlers, background work, streaming, runtime limits, and scheduled jobs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n\n## routing-middleware\n\nVercel routing and middleware behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review request routing, redirects, rewrites, and middleware boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/routing-middleware/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-best-practices\n\nReact and TSX quality checklist for structure, hooks, accessibility, performance, and types.\n\nWhen to use: Review React components, hooks, client boundaries, rendering behavior, or TSX performance.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## shadcn\n\nOfficial shadcn component composition and project guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review UI built with shadcn components, registries, presets, forms, or component composition.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/shadcn/SKILL.md)\n\n## accessibility\n\nWCAG 2.2 accessibility guidance for web interfaces.\n\nWhen to use: Review semantics, keyboard use, focus, contrast, screen reader behavior, or accessibility acceptance criteria.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/accessibility/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-elements\n\nAI Elements guidance and local component references.\n\nWhen to use: Review a UI that depicts or controls an AI run, its steps, messages, or tool output.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-elements/SKILL.md)\n\n## reference-led-design\n\nThe owner's accepted design method: verbatim owner words, a screenshot board with his verdicts, acceptance criteria, distinct directions, image-anchored building.\n\nWhen to use: Propose or judge visual directions, explain what the owner responded to in reference screenshots, or extend an accepted design. Lanes use steps 1 to 4 read-only and cite board images.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/reference-led-design/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase\n\nSupabase guidance for Auth, SSR clients, RLS, and database changes.\n\nWhen to use: Review Supabase queries, Auth, RLS, migrations, client initialization, and ownership boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase-postgres-best-practices\n\nSupabase Postgres schema, SQL, RLS, and performance guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review tables, indexes, policies, RPCs, queries, and migrations.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-sdk\n\nVercel AI SDK generation, structured output, tool, and streaming guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model calls, output validation, tools, streaming, and provider integration.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-sdk/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-gateway\n\nVercel AI Gateway routing, model, and cost guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Gateway model identifiers, routing, limits, usage, cost, and failure handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-gateway/SKILL.md)\n\n## typesafe-ai\n\nTypeSafe Jev judgment and typed answer guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Jev questions, scoring contracts, response validation, and judgment use.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/typesafe-ai/SKILL.md)\n\n## prompt-format\n\nDraft assistant proposal for Oparax prompt and Jev question format; it is not an approved project rule.\n\nWhen to use: Consult when reviewing prompts, tool descriptions, untrusted data markers, or Jev questions. Treat its rules as nonbinding unless an approved plan or task explicitly adopts them.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/prompt-format/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-integration\n\nPostHog client and server initialization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review analytics SDK setup, identity, capture configuration, and duplicate initialization.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-integration/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-product-analytics\n\nPostHog product analytics guidance for meaningful user actions and identity.\n\nWhen to use: Review a feature or pull request for missing, duplicate, unsafe, or inconsistent product analytics.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-product-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-error-tracking\n\nPostHog error tracking setup and capture guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review server and client error capture, grouping, and sensitive data handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-error-tracking/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-feature-flags\n\nPostHog feature flag instrumentation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review feature flag evaluation, rollout behavior, and analytics when flags are in scope.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-feature-flags/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-llm-analytics\n\nPostHog AI observability guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model spans, token and cost capture, latency, and safe trace properties.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-llm-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-best-practices\n\nStripe integration and subscription guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review checkout, subscriptions, webhooks, idempotency, and key handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-docs\n\nStripe documentation lookup guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Stripe API assumptions against shipped guidance and official public docs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-docs/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-bits-pro\n\nLicensed React Bits Pro catalog, source integration, entitlement and harmonization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review React Bits Pro component or block choices and supplied source. Reviewers inspect files only; installation instructions do not grant install or MCP access.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-bits-pro/SKILL.md)\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":180,"fileSize":6315,"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-login-oct5/review-guidance/index.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":180},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"Read_1_82fe1b74-007c1","startedAtMs":"1791172996716","completedAtMs":"1791172997203"},"model_call_id":"5fbf36a4-1b05-4f94-8484-67282dce0a41-0-rj70","session_id":"c45b5518-a766-440e-9a99-d1e0e1c465be","timestamp_ms":1791172997218}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"Read_0_26fdf957-007c1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-login-oct5/brief.sent.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"TIME BUDGET: you have 10 minutes of wall time in total, counted from now; the runner stops you at 15. Plan the reading so you start writing by minute 7. Open at most 6 pictures unless the brief names fewer; read the rest by their descriptions. Deliver what you have by minute 10: a complete answer on time beats a perfect one late, and an answer that never arrives counts as nothing.\n\n# Council brief: what fills the right side of the login page with life (October 5, 2026, 00:25). Astra, Gemini Pro, Grok, Kimi, Muse. Under 450 words each. Read-only.\n\nThe owner, verbatim, on pass 14's login (p14-login.png): \"absolutely hate the effect this center flow produces. Despise it. But then what do I fill the right side with to add life? Cause I am extremely confused.\"\n\n## What he has said about the login before (verbatim, from focus-review/history/owner-history.md and PAGE-NOTES.md)\n- Oct 3: \"Continue with X. Continue with Google. Email, password. That's it.\" The form order is locked: email and password first, blue Log in, \"New to Oparax? Sign up\" swapping Confirm password in place, then neutral X and Google.\n- Oct 3, on React Bits auth blocks: \"auth5, auth4, auth3, and even auth1 as pretty neat designs.\"\n- Oct 4 18:05: \"I'm unhappy with the login. I'm still not liking it. I like the login for the Deck more than the current one, and I don't know why. I think your way of separating the login from the cards is not nice. Can you please look at some React Bits Pro component for the login and put it there?\"\n- Oct 4 20:10, on an orbit of the Oparax mark with slogan chips: \"you've put oparax's blue logo. If I say okay to that also, you could have put multiple different social media around it in the circle, right, or you could have put the card there.\"\n- Oct 4 21:15, on an orbit of real logos around a story card: \"the login is horrible. You just need to take reactbits pro and do the center flow simply. 1 story in the middle show its center flow coming in from github product hunt web rss and X that is it. And then the login card can become like it was before, looks neater but stick to our colors and accents.\"\n- Oct 4 21:30, his general complaint: \"You have so many fucking React bits and components. I hate it.\" And the rule the councils settled: when he names a real object, that object goes in the frame; nothing from a catalog stands in for it; objects about one thing are one object.\n- What makes a page alive for him (Oct 4): \"if it weren't for you adding the Vercel, Hugging Face, and all those logos on the left, it would have never looked so lively.\" The three originals he loves: deck-feed.png, window-feed.png, newsroom-feed.png.\n\n## Pictures (open in this order, at most 6)\n/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/renders/p14-login.png (now: Deck's card left, Center Flow right: the Next.js story in the centre, five source nodes, blue pulses; he despises the effect), deck-login.png (Deck's own login: the card with a fan of three story cards behind it, the version he said he likes more), p13-login.png (the orbit he rejected), p12-login.png (the rings with the mark he rejected), accepted-deck.png (the feed that sets the bar), p14-feed.png (the app the login opens into).\n\n## The fixed frame\nThe login page: the One header line (mark, wordmark, theme), Deck's independent lifted 420px form card at the left, the fixed dark/light theme (DESIGN.md), desktop only. The right side is the question. Code: site/v2/one/login.tsx, site/v2/one/card.tsx (the story card), site/v2/deck/data.ts (real sample stories with images and logos), site/v2/deck/marks.tsx (the real company marks).\n\n## Questions\n1. Why did Center Flow fail for him, in one line each from his words: the effect itself (pulses, glow, a diagram), the frame (a tech-demo object next to a product), or the objects (a diagram of sources is not the product).\n2. The right side: give TWO options, ranked, each a concrete composition in 5 lines: what objects (only real ones: his story cards with their pictures, the real company marks, the feed itself, the brief, nothing invented), how they are arranged relative to the 420px form, what moves if anything (and whether nothing should move), how it reads as \"this is what you get\" rather than decoration, and what it must not become (a fan that competes with the form; a dimmed backdrop; a catalog block). Say whether Deck's own fan (deck-login.png) is the answer as it stands, and if not, what is wrong with it in his words.\n3. The one you would build, and the one sentence the host should hold while building it.\n\nDeliver: RESULT: FINDINGS, then 1 to 3. No em dashes. Plain words; he reads this.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":28,"fileSize":4666,"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-login-oct5/brief.sent.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":28},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"Read_0_26fdf957-007c1","startedAtMs":"1791172996674","completedAtMs":"1791172997204"},"model_call_id":"5fbf36a4-1b05-4f94-8484-67282dce0a41-0-rj70","session_id":"c45b5518-a766-440e-9a99-d1e0e1c465be","timestamp_ms":1791172997234}
